**/*.pyc
**/cert
**/cred
**/.DS_Store

# Virtual environments.
# Current convention: per-OS environments created in the workspace root, named
# .venv-linux (Linux or WSL), .venv-macos (macOS), and .venv-win (Windows), so a
# single checkout on a drive shared between Windows 11 and WSL can hold a
# distinct venv for each host. The .venv* glob (no trailing slash) ignores that
# family, and the plain .venv default, both as top-level names and as path
# prefixes. The remaining entries are legacy environment names, kept ignored for
# existing local checkouts.
.venv*
**/venv
**/wsl-venv
**/piot-venv
.winvenv
